      "description": "The shared shape for `RespondToWorkRequest`, `SubmitSteeringInput`, `InvokeTool`, `InvokeApp`, `StartWorkflow`, `StartAgentRun`, `ReviseArtifact` and `PlaceArtifactVersion`. Every one of these commands triggers or responds to execution owned entirely by another authority (App, Workflow, Agent, Tool or Artifact ownership); Chat contributes only the triggering Message context, a `TargetReference` and a bounded opaque `input`, and never originates operation semantics for the referenced authority (freeze §7).",
